.TH SNIPARINJECT-SETTINGS 5 2026-11-28 "sniparinject" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
sniparinject-settings \- settings file of the SniParInject network sniffer and parser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
Network:
  interface: \fIname\fP | offline: \fIcapture file\fP
Server:
  protocol: tcp | udp
  ip: \fIaddress\fP
  port: \fInumber\fP
Game:
  host | node:
    display_message: Yes | No
    actions:
      \fIpacket id\fP:
        title: \fItext\fP
        display_message: Yes | No
        variable_length: Yes | No
        structs:
          \- name: \fItext\fP
            type: \fIstruct type\fP
            size: \fInumber\fP
            reference: \fImapping\fP
            output:
              type: hex | text
              zero_fill: \fInumber\fP
              auto_zero_fill: Yes | No
              fill: \fInumber\fP
              fill_left: \fInumber\fP
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
SniParInject reads the packets between this computer and a server, from a
network interface or from a capture file, and prints one line for each
packet that the settings describe.
The settings are a YAML file, usually named
.IR settings.yml ,
given to the
.B NetworkSniffer
class:
.PP
.EX
from sniparinject.network_sniffer import NetworkSniffer

NetworkSniffer(\(aqsettings.yml\(aq).start()
.EE
.PP
The file is read again when it changes on disk, so the rules of the
.B Game
section can be edited while the sniffer runs.
When the sniffer starts it checks the file and stops with a list of every
problem found (see
.BR DIAGNOSTICS ).
Keys that are not described here are allowed, for example a key that only
holds YAML anchors.
.SH NETWORK
The optional
.B Network
mapping tells where the packets come from.
.TP
.BI interface: " name"
The network interface to sniff, for example
.BR enp4s0 .
List them with
.B ip addr
or
.BR "ls /sys/class/net" .
Sniffing an interface needs root permissions.
.TP
.BI offline: " file"
Read the packets from a
.B pcap
or
.B pcapng
capture file instead of an interface.
A relative path is relative to the settings file.
It does not need root permissions.
Only the packets to or from the
.B Server
address and port are parsed.
.SH SERVER
The
.B Server
mapping is required.
It selects the connection to read; set
.BR ip ,
.B port
or both.
.TP
.BI protocol: " tcp | udp"
The transport protocol, in any letter case.
The default is
.BR tcp .
.TP
.BI ip: " address"
The IP address of the server.
.TP
.BI port: " number"
The port of the server, from 1 to 65535.
.PP
Find them with
.B lsof \-i
or
.BR "netstat \-nap" .
.PP
With
.BR tcp ,
the segments of each direction are joined in sequence order and the
retransmitted bytes are skipped, so a game packet split across segments is
parsed once it is complete.
After a lost segment the stream starts again from the next one.
.SH GAME
The
.B Game
mapping is required and needs a
.B host
or a
.B node
mapping, or both.
.B host
describes the packets that the server sends, printed after
.BR "<\-\-" .
.B node
describes the packets that this computer sends, printed after
.BR "\-\->" .
Each one accepts:
.TP
.BI display_message: " Yes | No"
Print the actions of this side.
The default is
.BR Yes .
An action can override it.
.TP
.BI actions: " mapping"
The actions, keyed by packet id.
.SS Actions
A game packet starts with its id, an
.B unsigned short
(2 bytes, little-endian): the raw bytes
.B 7d 00
are the id
.BR 0x7d .
The key of an action is that id as a YAML number, for example
.B 0x7d
or
.BR 125 ;
a quoted id such as
.B \(aq0x7d\(aq
is text and is an error.
An action with no properties prints only the direction arrow.
.TP
.BI title: " text"
The text printed after the direction arrow.
.TP
.BI display_message: " Yes | No"
Print this action.
When it is missing, the value of the side is used.
.TP
.BI variable_length: " Yes | No"
The two bytes after the id are the total length of the packet, including
the id and the length (an
.BR "unsigned short" ).
The length is printed as
.BR Length ,
the
.B structs
parse the body, and the bytes of the body that the
.B structs
do not take are printed in hex as
.BR Data .
.TP
.BI structs: " list"
How to split the bytes after the id, in order.
Without
.BR variable_length ,
the size of the packet is 2 plus the size of its structs, and the next
packet starts right after it.
.PP
An unknown id takes all the data left, because its size is not known.
Define the actions of the packets that come before the ones you study.
.SS Structs
.TP
.BI name: " text"
A label printed before the value.
.TP
.BI type: " struct type"
Required.
How to read the value; see
.BR "STRUCT TYPES" .
.TP
.BI size: " number"
How many times the type repeats, 0 or more.
For
.B chars
it is the number of bytes: a
.B chars
of
.B size: 24
is one 24 bytes value.
.TP
.BI reference: " mapping"
A mapping from values to text.
A value found in it is printed as its text; any other value is printed as
usual.
It is usually a YAML alias of a mapping defined elsewhere in the file:
.RS
.PP
.EX
Game:
  node:
    references:
      shop_options: &shop_options
        0x0: Buy
        0x1: Sell
    actions:
      0xc5:
        title: Shop store
        structs:
          \- name: ID
            type: unsigned char
            reference: *shop_options
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI output: " mapping"
How to print the value; see
.BR Output .
.SS Output
.TP
.BI type: " hex | text"
.B hex
prints a number as
.B 0x
and hex digits, and bytes as hex digits.
.B text
decodes bytes as UTF\-8 up to the first zero byte, which suits the names
padded with zeros.
Without a type, the value is printed as Python prints it, for example
.BR b\(aq\ex00\ex0f\(aq .
.TP
.BI zero_fill: " number"
Add zeros to the left until the value has this width.
For a hex value the zeros go after the
.B 0x
prefix:
.B 0x12
with a width of 8 is
.BR 0x000012 .
.TP
.BI auto_zero_fill: " Yes | No"
Add zeros to the left up to the width of the struct type: an
.B unsigned int
(4 bytes) in hex is printed with 8 digits, for example
.BR 0x00000005 .
.TP
.BI fill: " number"
Add spaces to the right until the value has this width.
.TP
.BI fill_left: " number"
Add spaces to the left until the value has this width.
.SH STRUCT TYPES
The values of
.B type
in a struct, in any letter case, with the symbol of the Python
.B struct
module and the size in bytes.
All the values are read in little-endian order.
.PP
.TS
l l l.
Type	Symbol	Bytes
char	c	1
signed char	b	1
unsigned char	B	1
bool	?	1
short	h	2
unsigned short	H	2
int	i	4
unsigned int	I	4
long	q	8
unsigned long	Q	8
half precision	e	2
float	f	4
double	d	8
chars	s	1
.TE
.SH OUTPUT
Each packet is printed on standard output as one line of fields that end
with
.BR | ,
for example:
.PP
.EX
<\-\- Being name | ID 0x068e9f12 | Name Bob |
.EE
.PP
The colors tell
.B host
lines from
.B node
lines.
A packet with an id that has no action is printed, when its side displays
messages, as the side, the id and the data left in hex, followed by a line
with the whole raw data:
.PP
.EX
HOST | ID 0x7f | 1a2b3c
     |\-> 7f001a2b3c
.EE
.PP
Parse errors, for example a packet shorter than its structs, are written
to standard error with the raw data, and the sniffer goes on with the next
packet.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When the sniffer starts it stops with
.B SettingsError
and a list of every problem when:
.BR Server " or " Game
is missing,
.B Game
has neither
.B host
nor
.BR node ,
.B protocol
is not
.BR tcp " or " udp ,
a section, action, struct,
.B output
or
.B reference
is not a mapping,
.B structs
is not a list,
a packet id is not a number,
a struct
.B type
is unknown,
a
.B size
is not a number of 0 or more,
or
.BR zero_fill ,
.BR fill " or " fill_left
is not a number.
A
.B port
that is not a number from 1 to 65535 also stops it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print the packets of a game server on port 5122:
.PP
.EX
%YAML 1.1
\-\-\-
Network:
  interface: enp4s0

Server:
  ip: 52.174.196.146
  port: 5122

Game:
  node:
    actions:
      0x7d:
        title: Scenario change
      0x85:
        title: Player move to
        structs:
          \- type: chars
            size: 3
            output:
              type: hex
  host:
    actions:
      0x78:
        title: NPC Info
        structs:
          \- name: ID
            type: unsigned int
            output:
              type: hex
              auto_zero_fill: Yes
          \- name: HP
            type: unsigned short
.EE
.PP
The bytes
.B 85 00 a0 7f 18
sent by this computer print
.BR "\-\-> Player move to | a07f18 |" .
.PP
Parse a capture recorded with
.BR tshark ,
without root:
.PP
.EX
tshark \-i enp4s0 \-f \(aqtcp port 5122\(aq \-w capture.pcapng
.EE
.PP
.EX
Network:
  offline: capture.pcapng
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tshark (1),
.BR pcap (3PCAP),
.UR https://docs.python.org/3/library/struct.html#format-characters
the Python struct module
.UE ,
